LUMINA CITY – THE HEART OF THE EMPIRE OF LIGHT
16:9 NEO‑UKIYO‑E MASTERPIECE
(Urban Layout Map with Aurelius II, King Aurelius II, Tigreal, Silvanna, Alucard, Granger, Fanny, Lancelot, Odette & Old Man Hennessey)
1. REFERENCE IMAGE & GEOGRAPHICAL FIDELITY

Take the uploaded Moniyan Empire regional map as an absolute geographical stencil for Lumina City. Zoom into the centre‑left heart of the empire, where the capital gleams like a golden jewel at the nexus of the Moniyan Plains, the Imperial Roads, and the sacred river flowing from the Azure Lake. Maintain with surgical precision:

The city’s position relative to the Azure Lake (south‑east, a distant shimmer)

Castle Grandrock (north, a fortress atop a colossal plateau)

Castle Aberleen (south, shrouded in pale mist)

Castle Gorge (west, the western capital)

The Moniyan Plains (stretching west and east)

The Imperial Road (a golden artery connecting the capital to the empire)

Do not alter, move, or distort the city’s seven holy gates, its concentric ring layout, the Oracle Plaza at its heart, or the Cathedral of Light’s twin spires. Lumina City must sit exactly where it is placed on your reference map. The only transformation permitted is a massive increase in detail to render the capital as a fully realised, living metropolis with:

The Divine Palace Quarter (Aurelius II, King Aurelius II, the imperial throne, royal guard barracks, gardens, stables)

The Cathedral of Light & Sanctuary Quarter (the grand cathedral, cloisters, reliquary, bell tower, Monastery of Light exarchs)

The Lightborn Citadel (Silvanna’s headquarters, Lightborn Chevalier barracks, training yard, armory, council chamber)

The Imperial Garrison (Tigreal’s command, elite Imperial Knight barracks, parade ground, watchtower, Alucard, Granger, and Fanny)

The Oracle Plaza (sacred obelisk, pilgrim crowds, celestial griffins, divine light beams)

The Radiant Market District (the Grand Market, artisans’ quarter, the Ember Cellar forge, Old Man Hennessey)

The Lakeside Palaces (Lancelot’s Baroque manse, Odette’s Swan Lake promenade, noble estates, weeping willows)

The Seven Holy Gates (each dedicated to a virtue, with unique architecture and guard detachments)

Dozens of tiny citizen, guard, knight, pilgrim, and merchant silhouettes – visible at a human scale, each distinct

Ten legendary heroes placed as tiny, visible figures throughout the city

The result must feel like a sacred, illuminated cartographic scroll – as if commissioned by the Emperor himself and painted by the master cartographers of the Radiant Order, using ink infused with gold dust, crushed sapphires, and holy water. All landmarks are labelled in elegant English cartographic script, with Japanese calligraphy for the poetic title and invocation.

2. CANVAS & COMPOSITION

Generate a 16:9 horizontal image (1920×1080 pixels).

Lumina City is a radial, concentric metropolis built around the sacred Oracle Plaza. Seven grand boulevards radiate outward from the centre like spokes of a divine wheel, each terminating at one of the Seven Holy Gates. The city is ringed by a magnificent curtain wall of white stone and gold trim. The composition is a bird’s‑eye / isometric urban layout, oriented with north at the top, south at the bottom, west on the left, east on the right.

Urban tiers (concentric rings from centre outward) :

Centre (0‑200px radius) : The Sacred Heart – Oracle Plaza, the Obelisk of Prophecy, the Divine Palace of the Moniyan Throne, the Cathedral of Light.

Inner Ring (200‑400px radius) : The Noble Quarter – Lightborn Citadel (Silvanna’s headquarters, Lightborn barracks), Imperial Garrison (Tigreal’s command, elite barracks, Alucard, Granger, Fanny), noble estates (Lancelot’s Baroque manse, Odette’s Swan Lake promenade).

Middle Ring (400‑600px radius) : The Radiant Market District – merchant guilds, artisans’ quarters, the Ember Cellar forge (Old Man Hennessey), inns, taverns, bathhouses.

Outer Ring (600‑800px radius) : The Common Ward – residential districts, lesser shrines, small parks, pilgrim hostels, trade depots, city guard barracks.

Boundary (800‑900px radius) : The Curtain Wall – seven towering Holy Gates, garrison towers, watch platforms, the Luminous River moat.

Cardinal axes :

North‑South Axis (vertical) : The Imperial Way – from the northern Gate of Vigil (toward Castle Grandrock) to the southern Gate of Mercy (toward Castle Aberleen).

East‑West Axis (horizontal) : The Golden Processional – from the eastern Gate of Dawn (toward the Monastery of Light) to the western Gate of Hope (toward the Radiant Sea).

The entire composition is presented as a gilded, illuminated cartographic scroll – as if painted by master scribes of the Radiant Order using ink infused with gold dust and holy water. All landmarks and character placements are labelled in elegant English cartographic script with gold, silver, or sepia shadows depending on the district.

3. STYLE: NEO‑UKIYO‑E WITH SUMI‑E INK WASH (THE AESTHETIC OF THE DIVINE CAPITAL)

The map is rendered in an uncompromising fusion of Neo‑Ukiyo‑e woodblock aesthetics and Zen Sumi‑e ink‑wash techniques, adapted for the holiest and most prosperous city in the Land of Dawn, where every building seems to be touched by the Lord of Light himself.

Brushwork specifications :

Buildings : Precise, architectural strokes – straight lines for walls (1‑2px), curved lines for domes and cathedral roofs, tiny repeating strokes for shingles and cobblestones. The architectural style is high‑Gothic and Neoclassical, with flying buttresses, rose windows, spires, and colonnades.

City walls : Heavy, fortified lines – double‑layered with crenellations (small vertical strokes), interrupted by massive gatehouses. The walls are 10px thick, with tiny arrow slits visible every 10px.

Plazas : Open, pale washes – the Oracle Plaza is a perfect circle of luminous ivory with a golden obelisk at its centre. The plaza stones are individually drawn as tiny grey rectangles.

Canals (Luminous River) : Flowing, wet‑on‑wet washes of pale cerulean and silver, with tiny bridges (arched strokes) crossing at intervals. The water is dotted with tiny white swan silhouettes.

Trees and gardens : Soft, layered washes – emerald and viridian for parks, pale pink for cherry blossoms, deep green for cypress trees, pale gold for weeping willows.

Warrior, guard, pilgrim, merchant silhouettes : Each is a tiny, masterful single‑stroke figure (2‑4mm tall). Distinguish by:

Imperial Knights : Plate armour, capes, halberds, golden crests on their shields.

Lightborn Chevaliers : Elaborate white‑and‑gold armour, radiant halos (tiny gold circles), glowing weapons.

City Guards : Chainmail, spears, blue capes, silver helmets.

Pilgrims : Hooded robes, walking staves, prayer beads.

Merchants : Tunics, aprons, pushing carts, some with scales (justice).

Nobles : Fine robes, hats, carrying canes or parasols.

Commoners : Simple tunics, carrying baskets or water jugs.

Raised lacquer details (3D texture effects) :

The Divine Palace : Raised 24K gold leaf for the throne‑room dome and the royal crest (a golden griffin rampant). Raised silver for the palace’s colonnades and statues.

The Oracle Obelisk : Raised gold and silver lacquer for the prophetic runes that spiral up its length. Raised translucent white for the divine light beam that shoots from its peak.

The Cathedral of Light : Raised gold for the twin spires, raised silver for the rose window, raised ruby and sapphire lacquer for the stained‑glass details. Raised bronze for the great doors.

The Lightborn Citadel : Raised matte silver for the armoury, raised gold for the Lightborn crest (a winged sunburst).

The Seven Holy Gates : Raised gold for the gate names, raised silver for the virtue‑symbols above each arch.

The Luminous River : Raised translucent silver for the water’s surface, with tiny overlapping wave crests.

Parchment base : A radiant, sun‑bleached ivory washi with a subtle golden shimmer (achieved by a faint yellow‑gold wash across the entire parchment). The parchment has a faint, ghostly impression of a celestial griffin watermark visible when held to light. Paper fibres are visible as very fine, pale lines.

Texture fidelity : 8K‑grade. Every building, every cobblestone, every stained‑glass window, every tower, every bridge, and every tiny hero silhouette must be crisp, tangible, and geometrically perfect. No smudging, no warping, no AI deformities.

4. THE NEO‑UKIYO‑E BORDER — THE RADIANT RELIQUARY

The map is enclosed in a single, majestic, 50‑pixel‑wide border befitting the Empire of Light, functioning as a holy reliquary containing the symbols of the imperial faith.

Outermost edge (6px) : A hairline of burnished 24K gold leaf, slightly irregular and luminous, gleaming under imagined celestial light. It has tiny, raised points of pale blue (like divine sparks) at 2‑cm intervals.

First inner register (18px) : A continuous frieze of stylised Gothic arch motifs rendered in raised gold lacquer, each arch framing a tiny, silver Radiant Order cross (a central cross with four smaller crosses in each quadrant). Between the arches, celestial griffin feathers in dry‑brush charcoal sumi, each quill a single, masterful stroke.

Second inner register (20px) : A flowing band of stylised sunbursts and holy flames, rendered in raised gold and translucent orange‑amber lacquer. The sunbursts radiate outward; the flames lick upward toward the corners. This band represents the eternal light of the Lord of Light.

Third inner register (6px) : A line of tiny, individually painted golden suns – each a 3px circle with eight radiating rays. There are 72 of them around the entire border, representing the 72 Divine Laws of the Moniyan Creed.

Four corners — ornate compass medallions (each 40px x 40px) :

Northwest corner : The Moniyan Imperial Crown – a golden crown with three prominent spires (the central spire tallest), set with a central sapphire (blue dot), wreathed in olive branches (green strokes). Represents the authority of the Moniyan throne.

Northeast corner : The Sword of the Radiant Order – a longsword point‑up, with wings emerging from the crossguard, surrounded by seven stars (gold dots). Represents the martial might of the Lightborn.

Southwest corner : The Shield of Faith – a kite‑shield with a golden griffin rampant, the symbol of the Imperial Guard. The shield is edged with silver.

Southeast corner : The Orb of Light – a crystalline sphere with a glowing core (pale yellow dot), encircled by a ring of runes (tiny silver symbols), representing the Lord of Light’s eternal watch over the empire.

Innermost edge (4px) : A soft, unbroken enso circle of warm ivory‑gold sumi, its stroke smooth and continuous — representing the eternal, unbreakable light of the Empire of Light. The brush stroke is 6px wide with a gentle gradient from pale gold to warm ivory.

Border colour palette : Burnished gold, raised silver, warm amber, translucent orange, deep charcoal, pale ivory, sapphire blue, and ruby red.

5. THE LANDSCAPE — ZOOMED‑IN, HYPER‑DETAILED LUMINA CITY

Lumina City is a radial, concentric metropolis organised around the sacred Oracle Plaza. The city has seven districts, each with its own character, architecture, and legendary inhabitants. The city’s population is represented by hundreds of tiny silhouettes – knights, guards, pilgrims, merchants, nobles, commoners.

5.1 The Divine Palace Quarter (Centre‑North) – The Seat of the Moniyan Throne

Location: North of the Oracle Plaza, occupying the highest ground in the city, on a gentle hill that overlooks the entire capital.

Architectural style: White marble, gold trim, soaring domes, arched colonnades, stained‑glass windows depicting the history of the Moniyan dynasty. The palace complex is a city within a city, surrounded by a fortified inner wall with golden griffin statues at every gate.

Key buildings (labelled) :

The Moniyan Imperial Palace (The Radiant Keep) : A magnificent complex of white marble and gold, with a central keep whose towering spire (60px tall) pierces the sky. The spire is tipped with a massive, glowing golden crystal (8px diameter) that casts a gentle, perpetual light over the entire city – visible as a soft, translucent gold‑white halo (80px diameter). The throne room is visible through an arched window on the keep’s central face, with a golden throne and a massive crystal chandelier.

The Royal Balcony : A high balcony (20px wide) overlooking the Oracle Plaza, with a golden railing. Aurelius II – The King of Moniyan stands here (4mm tall). Distinguishing features:

Crown of Solis (Halo of the Eternal Light) : A crown with sharp, needle‑like rays (gold strokes) fanning behind his head.

Platinum‑blonde hair (pale gold strokes, long and wavy).

White‑and‑gold royal robes with ermine trim (tiny white zig‑zags on the hem).

Scepter of Absolute Radiance (tall gold staff with a diamond‑shaped, glowing crystal head).

Standing still, gazing out over his kingdom, one hand on the railing.

King Aurelius II (Prince Aurelius III – The Grandson) : A smaller figure beside his father (2.5mm tall), standing at the railing. Distinguishing features:

Smaller golden circlet (simple gold band, 2px wide).

White tunic with gold sash.

Ceremonial sword at his hip (thin silver line).

Looking up at his father.

The Throne Room : Visible through an arched window (15px wide, 10px tall) – a golden throne (a tall chair with a high back), royal banners (blue and gold rectangles hanging from the ceiling), and a massive crystal chandelier (tiny gold lines radiating from a central dot).

The Royal Gardens : Terraced gardens on the palace’s western slope, with fountains (pale blue ovals with water sprays), marble statues (tiny grey figures), and cherry blossom trees (pink clusters). Tiny gardener silhouettes (bent over, holding trowels) and noble silhouettes (fine robes, hats) stroll the paths.

The Royal Stables : A long, white‑stone building on the eastern side, 40px wide, 20px tall, with a row of tiny windows (yellow glows). Tiny white horse silhouettes (small ovals with legs) are visible inside.

The Palace Guard Barracks : A two‑story building attached to the palace’s southern wall, where the elite Palace Guard (the Praetorian Guard) is quartered. Tiny guard silhouettes (silver‑and‑blue armour, halberds) stand at attention outside.

Palace label : “Imperial Palace – The Radiant Keep”

Attack ministry : None directly – the palace is defended, not aggressive.

Defence ministry : The Palace Guard (Praetorian Guard) – 20 tiny Imperial Knight silhouettes in silver‑and‑blue armour, stationed at gates, patrolling the walls, guarding the throne room.

Character Placement :

Aurelius II – (960, 100) – Royal Balcony, standing, regal.

King Aurelius II (Prince Aurelius III) – (980, 115) – Royal Balcony, standing beside his father.

5.2 The Cathedral of Light & Sanctuary Quarter (Centre‑East)

Location: East of the Oracle Plaza, sharing the Sacred Heart ring.

Architectural style: Gothic masterpiece – flying buttresses, twin spires, a colossal circular rose window of ruby and sapphire glass, a bell tower with a golden bell, bronze doors carved with the history of the Moniyan faith.

Key buildings (labelled) :

The Cathedral of Light (Sanctum Lux) : The grandest temple in the empire. Twin spires rise 80px above the city, each tipped with a golden griffin statue (tiny gold silhouettes). The rose window is rendered as a circle of raised ruby and sapphire lacquer dots (3px each), 30px diameter, with a soft, translucent ruby‑and‑sapphire glow (40px diameter). The great doors are bronze (dark orange‑brown), carved with scenes of the Lord of Light’s triumph over the Abyss – visible as tiny carved figures (1px each).

The Cathedral Steps : A wide, sweeping staircase of white marble leading up to the great doors. Silvanna – The Imperial Knightess stands at the top of the steps (4mm tall). Distinguishing features:

Ash‑blonde ponytail (pale gold stroke) with a silver tiara.

White‑and‑blue tunic with silver breastplate.

Lance of Light (gold shaft, 20px tall, with a glowing cyan tip).

Standing at attention, holding her lance, facing the plaza.

The Cloisters : A quadrangle of arched walkways (a square of white stone with a central garden, 40px x 40px) surrounding a central garden with a holy well (pale blue oval, 10px diameter). Tiny monk and priest silhouettes (robes, tonsures – small bald heads with a circle of hair) walk the cloisters (8 total).

The Reliquary : A small, domed building attached to the cathedral’s north side, 20px diameter, where sacred artefacts are kept (including a shard of the True Light). A single, glowing golden light emanates from its window (soft yellow halo).

The Bell Tower : A square tower attached to the cathedral’s south side, 20px wide, 60px tall, with a massive bronze bell (golden oval) visible through an arched opening. A tiny bell‑ringer silhouette is visible inside.

Cathedral label : “Cathedral of Light – Sanctum Lux”

Attack ministry : None – this is a place of worship and healing.

Defence ministry : The Cathedral Guard – 8 tiny knight silhouettes (white armour, gold trim, halberds) stationed at the doors, the cloisters, and the bell tower.

Character Placement :

Silvanna – The Imperial Knightess – (1320, 250) – Cathedral steps, standing, holding her lance.

5.3 The Lightborn Citadel (Inner Ring – North‑East)

Location: North‑east of the Oracle Plaza, within the Noble Quarter, adjacent to the Cathedral of Light.

Architectural style: Fortified white‑and‑gold fortress – thick walls, battlements, a central keep with a golden Lightborn flag (a winged sunburst on a blue field). The citadel serves as the headquarters of the Lightborn Chevaliers – the empire’s most elite holy knights.

Key buildings (labelled) :

The Lightborn Citadel (Keep) : A central keep, 40px wide, 50px tall, with a golden flag flying from its highest tower. The walls are 5px thick, with arrow slits every 10px.

The Lightborn Barracks : A two‑story white‑stone building attached to the keep’s west side, 60px wide, 30px tall, with arched windows and a tiled roof. Inside, tiny Lightborn Chevalier silhouettes (white‑and‑gold armour, radiant halos – tiny gold circles behind their heads) are visible – 12 total, seated at a long table, reading scrolls, or sharpening swords.

The Armoury of the Lightborn : A squat, fortified building (30px wide, 20px tall) with a smoke vent, where Lightborn weapons are forged and maintained. Tiny smith silhouettes (2) are visible inside.

The Training Yard of the Lightborn : A large, open courtyard (60px wide, 40px tall) with wooden dummies (brown rectangles), weapon racks (wooden lines), and a duelling ring (a circle of pale stone). Tigreal – The Captain of the Imperial Knights stands at the yard’s centre, his massive warhammer planted, his shield raised (4mm tall). Distinguishing features:

Silver breastplate with golden sun crest (a small gold circle with rays).

Royal purple cape with golden bordering (flowing behind him).

Massive warhammer (Sunder‑Healer Sledge) (a 15px‑long grey head, 3px wide, with a glowing amber gem in its face).

Towering kite shield with central glowing orb (a 10px‑wide shield, pale grey with a glowing gold centre).

White hair, sharp jawline, piercing blue eyes (tiny blue dots).

Standing with his hammer planted, facing the training dummies.

The Council Chamber : A circular building (25px diameter) attached to the keep’s east side, where Lightborn officers plan campaigns. A round table with 6 tiny seated silhouettes (Lightborn captains) is visible through a window.

Citadel label : “Lightborn Citadel – Seat of the Lightborn Chevaliers”

Attack ministry : Lightborn training grounds, armory, war councils – the Lightborn are the empire’s offensive holy warriors.

Defence ministry : Citadel walls, garrisoned Lightborn knights, strategic location near the Cathedral and the eastern gate.

Character Placement :

Tigreal – The Captain of the Imperial Knights – (1120, 350) – Lightborn training yard, standing with hammer planted.

5.4 The Imperial Garrison (Inner Ring – North‑West)

Location: North‑west of the Oracle Plaza, within the Noble Quarter, adjacent to the northern wall.

Architectural style: Functional military complex – grey‑stone barracks, armoured gates, a parade ground, a tall watchtower. The Wertz family (Tigreal and Fanny’s noble house) has a wing here, but the garrison serves as the headquarters for the Imperial Knights – the regular military force of the empire.

Key buildings (labelled) :

The Garrison Keep : A square, grey‑stone keep, 30px wide, 40px tall, with the imperial banner (gold cross on white) flying from its tower. The walls are 4px thick.

The Imperial Barracks : A long, three‑story building, 80px wide, 30px tall, with rows of tiny windows (yellow glows). Elite Imperial Knights are quartered here – 20 tiny silhouettes visible through windows (sleeping, sitting, reading).

The Parade Ground : A wide, open stone square (80px wide, 60px tall) where soldiers drill. Alucard – The Demon Hunter stands at attention (4mm tall). Distinguishing features:

Deep navy long‑tailed duster coat (flowing behind him).

Silver‑winged brooch (glowing azure) on his right lapel.

Massive greatsword with skull crossguard (the sword is 25px long, with a skull-shaped crossguard – two small dark circles for eyes – and a glowing blue channel down its centre).

Right arm encased in a heavy silver gauntlet (containing his demonic corruption).

Dirty blonde hair, icy blue eyes (tiny blue dots).

Standing at attention, his greatsword resting on his shoulder.

Granger – The Death Chanter : Standing beside Alucard (4mm tall). Distinguishing features:

Black leather trench coat with high collar.

Violin‑case weapon (the “Requiem” cannon) slung across his back (a 15px‑long dark grey rectangle with a glowing red emblem – a small red dot – on its centre).

White hair with a black streak (tiny white and black strokes).

Pale skin, crimson‑eyed glare (tiny red dots).

Standing with his arms crossed, looking toward the northern gate.

Fanny – The Blade Dancer : Standing on the Watchtower platform (4mm tall). Distinguishing features:

Deep purple combat suit with vertical ribbing.

Gold‑trimmed collar, silver gauntlets.

Twin blades sheathed in iron‑like gear mechanisms on her hips (two small dark grey rectangles with gold dots – the grappling gear).

Golden‑yellow ponytail flaring upward (a small cluster of yellow strokes).

Crouched, one hand on her grappling gear, ready to launch her hook.

The Watchtower : A tall, square tower, 15px wide, 60px tall, with a brazier at the top (orange dot with pale yellow halo). Fanny stands on the platform at the top (see above).

The Garrison Armory : A fortified building (20px wide, 15px tall) attached to the keep’s west side, where Imperial Knight weapons and armour are stored.

Garrison label : “Imperial Garrison – Defenders of the Capital”

Attack ministry : Garrison training grounds, armory, watchtower, elite knight patrols – the Imperial Knights are the empire’s primary offensive military force.

Defence ministry : Garrison walls, watchtower, gatehouses, and the city’s main defensive wall.

Character Placement :

Alucard – The Demon Hunter – (400, 400) – Parade ground, standing at attention.

Granger – The Death Chanter – (430, 405) – Parade ground, standing beside Alucard.

Fanny – The Blade Dancer – (380, 280) – Watchtower platform, crouched, ready.

5.5 The Oracle Plaza (Sacred Heart – Centre)

Location: The absolute centre of Lumina City, at the intersection of the Imperial Way and the Golden Processional.

Architectural style: A vast, circular open space of polished white stone, inlaid with a golden compass rose (radiating outward in eight directions). The plaza is large enough (150px diameter) to hold tens of thousands of pilgrims and citizens. It is the spiritual and civic heart of the empire.

Key features (labelled) :

The Oracle’s Obelisk : A towering, needle‑like monument of gold‑veined white marble, 50px tall, at the exact centre of the plaza. Carved with prophetic runes in the ancient Moniyan script (tiny gold strokes spiralling up its length). A divine beam of light (translucent gold‑white shaft, 10px wide, 60px tall) pierces the sky above it, with a soft, translucent gold‑white halo (80px diameter) radiating outward.

Pilgrim Crowds : 50+ tiny pilgrim silhouettes (hooded robes, walking staves – thin brown lines) kneel in concentric rings around the obelisk, their faces raised toward the light. Some stand in long queues, waiting to touch the obelisk’s base.

Celestial Griffins : Two majestic celestial griffins (raised gold and silver lacquer, 30px wingspan each) circle the obelisk in a protective spiral, their forms a masterful, single‑stroke sumi wash of gold and pale ink.

Imperial Preachers : A few tiny priest silhouettes (white robes, tall hats) stand on small platforms (grey rectangles), preaching to the crowds.

Market Stalls : Temporary stalls set up around the plaza’s perimeter (at the edge of the inner ring), selling holy water (blue bottles), prayer scrolls (white rectangles), and small gold crosses (tiny gold shapes). Tiny merchant silhouettes (tunics, aprons) haggle with pilgrims.

Plaza label : “Oracle Plaza – Where the Light Speaks”

Defence ministry : The Plaza Guard – 8 tiny Imperial Knight silhouettes stationed around the plaza’s perimeter, maintaining order.

5.6 The Radiant Market District (Middle Ring – West & South‑West)

Location: West and south‑west of the Oracle Plaza, between the Noble Quarter and the western and southern Holy Gates.

Architectural style: Bustling, chaotic, colourful – timber‑framed buildings (brown with white plaster), tile roofs (red and brown), awnings in red, gold, and blue, open‑air markets, narrow alleys, and hidden courtyards. This district is the commercial heart of the city.

Key buildings (labelled) :

The Grand Market : A sprawling open‑air market with hundreds of stalls. Tiny merchant and buyer silhouettes haggle over spices (tiny red and brown piles), silks (rolls of coloured cloth), weapons (tiny grey shapes), and holy relics (small white rectangles). The sounds of haggling and coin‑counting are visualised as tiny gold coins (small circles) floating between hands.

The Artisans’ Quarter : A district of workshops – weavers (looms visible through open doors), potters (clay wheels, tiny grey pots), jewellers (tiny gold and silver shapes), armourers (small anvils, orange forge glows). Tiny artisan silhouettes (bent over, working) are visible.

The Ember Cellar (Old Man Hennessey’s Forge) : A hidden forge in the lowest level of the market district, accessible only through a narrow alley between two larger buildings. A single, small orange glow (furnace light, 10px diameter) emanates from a cellar door. Old Man Hennessey stands at the anvil, his massive sledgehammer raised (4mm tall). Distinguishing features:

Dragonskin‑Hide apron (dark grey, thick, with a heavy tool‑belt – small silver rectangles).

Bare, scarred arms, bulging veins (dark grey lines).

Massive sledgehammer (Sunder‑Healer) with meteorite iron head (a 10px‑long grey head, 4px wide, with jagged edges).

Brass‑rimmed industrial goggles pushed up on his brow (two small gold circles).

Steel‑grey beard, gruff, defiant posture, standing with his feet wide, hammer raised above his head.

The Pilgrim’s Rest Inn : A large, three‑story timber‑framed building with a sign depicting a sleeping pilgrim (a small silhouette on a bed). Tiny pilgrim silhouettes (hooded) are visible through the windows, eating and sleeping.

The Golden Tankard Tavern : A popular tavern with a golden tankard sign (a small gold cup). Tiny commoner silhouettes (simple tunics) are visible through the windows, drinking and laughing.

Market label : “Radiant Market District – The Heart of Commerce”

Defence ministry : City guard patrols (10 tiny guard silhouettes) in chainmail, carrying spears, walking through the market.

Attack ministry : Hidden – the Ember Cellar forges weapons for the “rejected” soldiers of the empire.

Character Placement :

Old Man Hennessey – (600, 650) – Ember Cellar, standing at his anvil, hammer raised.

5.7 The Lakeside Palaces (Inner Ring – South)

Location: South of the Oracle Plaza, overlooking the artificial canals leading to the Azure Lake. This district is home to the empire’s wealthiest noble families, including House Baroque and House Alvin (Odette’s family).

Architectural style: Elegant, pastoral – white marble palaces, arched bridges over silver water, weeping willow trees (drooping green and pale gold washes), swan‑spirit groves.

Key buildings (labelled) :

The Baroque Manse (Lancelot’s Family Estate) : A white marble mansion, 50px wide, 40px tall, with a central dome (gold) and a fountain in the courtyard (pale blue oval with water sprays). The manse has a fencing piste (a long, narrow strip of pale stone) in the garden, where Lancelot – The Perfumed Knight practices (4mm tall). Distinguishing features:

Deep chocolate‑brown tunic, open at the chest.

Sapphire‑blue capelet flowing behind him.

Golden‑blonde hair flowing in waves (pale gold strokes).

Rapier with golden bell guard (a thin silver line for the blade, a small gold circle for the bell guard).

Red rose petals drifting around him (tiny red dots).

Standing in a fencing stance, his rapier extended in a lunge.

The Swan Lake Promenade (Odette’s Estate) : A terraced garden with a small, artificial lake (pale blue oval, 30px diameter) where white swans drift (tiny white dots). A white marble pavilion (curved roof, gold trim) stands at the water’s edge. Odette – The Swan Princess stands on the pavilion’s balcony (4mm tall). Distinguishing features:

White‑and‑silver bodice, layered petal‑like skirt (white with silver lines).

Silver wing‑tiara (tiny silver arcs on her head).

Ivory staff with crescent‑shaped head (a pale white staff, 15px tall, with a silver crescent at the top enclosing a glowing blue crystal).

Strawberry‑blonde hair cascading in waves (pale orange strokes).

Three spectral swan‑spirits (pale cyan strokes, 10px wingspan each) circling her.

Standing with her staff in one hand, her other hand outstretched.

The Weeping Willow Grove : A grove of ancient weeping willow trees (drooping green and pale gold washes) along the canal’s edge, with tiny swan silhouettes (white dots) swimming in the water.

The Canal Bridges : Three arched bridges (each 20px long) cross the canals, connecting the noble estates to the main city.

Palaces label : “Lakeside Palaces – Home of the Noble Houses”

Defence ministry : Private guards – 4 tiny guard silhouettes in the livery of House Baroque (blue and gold) and House Alvin (white and silver) at each estate’s gate.

Character Placement :

Lancelot – The Perfumed Knight – (1600, 720) – Baroque Manse garden, fencing stance.

Odette – The Swan Princess – (1400, 750) – Swan Lake Promenade, standing on the pavilion balcony.

5.8 The Seven Holy Gates (Outer Ring – Boundary)

Location: The boundary of the city, where the seven grand boulevards terminate at the curtain wall. Each gate is a towering structure (20px wide, 40px tall) with a gatehouse, guard barracks, and a portcullis (a grid of iron bars).

Each gate is unique (labelled) :

Gate of Vigil (North) : The largest gate, facing Castle Grandrock. Flanked by two golden griffin statues (raised gold lacquer, 10px tall each). The imperial banner (gold cross on white) flies from its towers.

Gate of Dawn (East) : Facing the Monastery of Light. Adorned with a massive golden sunburst (raised gold) on its archway. A constant stream of pilgrims enters through it.

Gate of Hope (West) : Facing the Radiant Sea. Adorned with a silver anchor (raised silver) on its archway, symbolising safe voyages.

Gate of Mercy (South) : Facing Castle Aberleen. Adorned with a weeping angel (raised silver) on its archway, symbolising compassion for the lost.

Gate of Justice (North‑East) : Adorned with silver scales (raised silver). The imperial courthouse is just inside it.

Gate of Wisdom (North‑West) : Adorned with an open book (raised gold). The Royal Library is nearby.

Gate of Fortitude (South‑East) : Adorned with a crossed sword and shield (raised silver). The main military depot is here.

Gatehouse guards : 4 tiny Imperial Knight silhouettes at each gate (28 total), standing at attention, holding halberds.

